Z||000000||theogre||05-22-2001||08:30 PM||||I've mentioned in other threads that the rear calipers can be a _____ to bleed. Especially after they are replaced or something that lets in lots of air.<P>This is a drawing that will eventually get added to a cave article but I thought you all might like to see it now. It's a colorized version of the line drawing in US Patent 4,181,145 by GM. (That patent covers the check valve in the face of the piston.)<P>The drawing gives you an idea why the caliper can trap so much air.... <P><BR>Also,,, If you are leaking fluid from the check valve..... The piston module is shot. It can't be fixed. You'll have to replace the piston or get a rebuilt caliper.<P> <IMG SRC="http://home.sprynet.com/~theogre/tunnel6/misc_files/rearcalcut.gif">  <BR><p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 05-22-2001).]||||reg||1
