Z||000003||SteveJ||05-23-2001||08:51 AM||||For those of us who have done rear brake work and replaced a caliper or two without problem, it appears we dodged the bullet. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||05-23-2001||11:08 AM||||I have to say,,, I was really suprised how much stuff is in the piston... There's another piston, a cam, a ball bearing, another heavy spring, and another seal...<P>What was really interesting is that the area between the pistons is a air space. The rubber "plug" in the face of the main piston is actually a valve that lets air in and out of that space while preventing dirt getting in.<P>I've been digging for a good picture/text of the "revised" pistons that don't have the plug to see how they are differant. So far no luck.<P>This b/w picture this is made from actually came from the patent on the check valve. I couldn't find one for the caliper. ||||reg||1
